					<div class="article__inner">
									<div class="article__content">
							
    <section class="main-content">
                    <div class="main-content__intro margin-trim type-body-xl">
                <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A journalist meets a man in a ruined village outside Kyiv.</span></p>
<p><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">Why don&#8217;t you start with when the war began for you?</span></i></p>

            </div>
        
                    <div class="main-content__text margin-trim type-body-l">
                <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Man from Stoyanka is a security guard, just an ordinary man. But when everyone else flees, he stays. As his home turns into a no man&#8217;s land, he chooses to take extraordinary action.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">And she&#8217;s there to record it &#8211; for the history books, for the courts, for humanity.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Playful and unsettling, Offie-nominated </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Reckoning</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> is a vivid and powerful new play about war, survival and the fragile trust between those who uncover the truth and those who must live with it.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Based on real events within The Reckoning Project&#8217;s verified archive of witness testimonies of the Russian war in Ukraine, each performance is followed by Food for Thought, a reflection from a journalist, lawyer or those with direct experience of the conflict.</span></p>

            </div>
            </section>

	<ul class="post-details post-details--event not-prose has-black-40-background-color rounded" role="list">        <li class="post-detail">
